<div class="privacy-container">
    <h1>@Model</h1>

    <div class="privacy-meta">
        <h2>Project Title: Computer Vision-Based Facial Recognition Attendance Using Machine Learning</h2>
        <p><strong>Institution:</strong> Universidad de Manila – College of Computing Studies<br /><strong>Project Type:</strong> Bachelor of Science in Information Technology Capstone Project</p>

        <p><strong>Researchers:</strong></p>
        <ul>
            <li>Elape, Hanz Jericho C.</li>
            <li>Garcia, Justin Vlady Rain C.</li>
            <li>Gonzaga, Edzell</li>
            <li>Sabiniano, Rain Justine G.</li>
        </ul>

        <p class="mb-0"><strong>Effective Date:</strong> May 2026</p>
    </div>

    <hr />

    <div class="privacy-body">
        <h2>1. Purpose of This Privacy Policy</h2>
        <p>This Privacy Policy explains how personal information is collected, used, stored, and protected in the Computer Vision-Based Facial Recognition Attendance Using Machine Learning system ("the System").</p>
        <p>The System is developed solely as an academic capstone project for research, demonstration, testing, and evaluation purposes. Its purpose is to explore the use of computer vision and machine learning for attendance recording and identity verification.</p>

        <h2>2. Information Collected</h2>
        <p>The System may collect the following information:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Name</li>
            <li>Student, employee, or participant identification number</li>
            <li>Course, section, department, or role</li>
            <li>Attendance date, time, and status</li>
            <li>Facial images captured during registration or attendance verification</li>
            <li>Face-verification result, match score, or confidence level</li>
            <li>System logs needed to identify errors, failed verification attempts, or possible misuse</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>3. Use of Information</h2>
        <p>Collected information will be used only to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Register participants in the System.</li>
            <li>Verify identity for attendance purposes.</li>
            <li>Record attendance, time-in, time-out, late status, or absence.</li>
            <li>Evaluate the accuracy and performance of the facial-recognition model.</li>
            <li>Improve the System as part of the capstone project.</li>
            <li>Prepare anonymized project results, documentation, and academic presentations.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Personal information and facial data will not be used for advertising, commercial purposes, unrelated profiling, or public disclosure.</p>

        <h2>4. Facial Data</h2>
        <p>Facial images and face-verification information are collected only when necessary for the System's attendance-verification function.</p>
        <p>The System may generate a face-match result or confidence level. If the confidence level is low or the identity cannot be verified, the attendance record may be marked for manual review. A low-confidence result does not automatically mean that a participant is absent or attempting to misuse the System.</p>
        <p>Facial images and verification records will not be sold, shared publicly, or used outside the academic purpose of this capstone project.</p>

        <h2>5. Consent</h2>
        <p>Before facial images or other personal information are collected, participants will be informed about the purpose of collection and asked for their consent where required.</p>
        <p>Participation in facial-recognition testing is voluntary. Participants may decline or withdraw their consent by contacting the researchers or project adviser. When feasible, an alternative attendance-recording method may be provided.</p>

        <h2>6. Access and Sharing</h2>
        <p>Access to personal information is limited to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>The listed student researchers;</li>
            <li>The project adviser and authorized faculty evaluators, when needed for academic evaluation; and</li>
            <li>Authorized participants responsible for testing or administering the System.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>Information will not be shared with third parties unless required by law, approved by the participant, or necessary for approved academic evaluation.</p>

        <h2>7. Data Storage and Security</h2>
        <p>Reasonable safeguards will be used to protect collected information, including restricted access, password-protected accounts, secure storage, and limited access to facial images and attendance records.</p>
        <p>Only authorized individuals involved in the project may access the System's data. The researchers will take reasonable steps to prevent unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, or disclosure of information.</p>

        <h2>8. Data Retention and Deletion</h2>
        <p>Personal information and facial data will be retained only for the duration necessary to complete the capstone project, testing, evaluation, and academic presentation requirements.</p>
        <p>After the project is completed, data will be securely deleted, anonymized, or retained only when required by Universidad de Manila policies or applicable law. Participants may request deletion of their data, subject to legitimate academic, technical, or legal requirements.</p>

        <h2>9. Participant Rights</h2>
        <p>Subject to applicable requirements, participants may request to:</p>
        <ul>
            <li>Know what personal information has been collected.</li>
            <li>Correct inaccurate or incomplete information.</li>
            <li>Withdraw consent for the use of their facial data.</li>
            <li>Request deletion of their information after the project requirements have been completed.</li>
            <li>Raise concerns regarding the collection, use, or protection of their information.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2>10. Compliance</h2>
        <p>The researchers intend to handle personal information in accordance with applicable privacy requirements, including the Philippine Data Privacy Act of 2012 (Republic Act No. 10173), its implementing rules, and applicable Universidad de Manila policies.</p>

